{
  "abstract": "We construct algebraic representatives of the exceptional determinant Hodge classes on the cube of an explicit non-CM K3 surface with real multiplication, and prove the rational Hodge conjecture on all its powers. Put $D_5(s)=s^5-5s^3+5s$ and let $X$ be the smooth minimal model of $y^2=x^3+3(D_5(s)-2)x+(D_5(s)-2)(D_5(s)-6)/2$. Fiber geometry, algebraic dihedral correspondences and independently checked finite-field counts prove $\\rho(X)=16$, $\\operatorname{End}_{\\mathrm{Hdg}}T(X)=\\mathbf Q(\\sqrt5)$ and rational Witt index one. We give an explicit degree-120 dominant map from the square of the genus-19 curve $w^{30}=v^{26}(1-v)^{15}(1+v)^5$ to $X$. An exact holomorphic pullback places the transcendental image in the primitive order-thirty Jacobian factor. Twisting one curve factor by an order-four automorphism identifies this image with a rank-six adjoint Hodge structure. A triangle of curve diagonals evaluates the alternating matrix trace and produces both real-multiplication determinant classes on $X^3$; orthogonal invariant theory gives all powers. We also determine the full Hodge group of the source abelian eightfold, including its center, and prove that divisor classes generate the Hodge rings of all its powers. The product map makes the motive of $X$ of abelian type and Kimura finite dimensional. Exact symbolic and arithmetic certificates are supplied. No canonical Kuga–Satake correspondence or general solution of the Hodge conjecture is asserted.",
